  "duration": 26.048,
  "text": "A robot built to last 90 days on Mars, kept going from more than 14 years. Dust should have choked its solar panels within months. Martian wind kept sweeping them clean. The team called them cleaning events. Each one gave the rover back its power and it kept driving. 90 days became years. Then in 2018, a storm wrapped the whole planet and the sky went dark.",
